      "id": 31,
      "formula_id": 10,
      "title": "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis: XYS for Anxiety Disorders (2022)",
      "description": "A meta-analysis of 9 randomized controlled trials with 809 patients found that Xiao Yao San, used alone or combined with conventional anxiolytic medications, showed greater improvement in anxiety symptoms and fewer adverse drug reactions compared to anxiolytic treatment alone. The authors noted that further high-quality research is needed to confirm these findings.",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35432568/",
      "periodical": "Lin J, Ji Y, et al. Evidence-Based Complementary and Alternative Medicine. 2022; Article ID 1319592."
    },
    {
      "id": 32,
      "formula_id": 10,
      "title": "Systematic Review with Meta-Analysis and Trial Sequential Analysis: XYS for Anxiety (2023)",
      "description": "This updated systematic review with trial sequential analysis confirmed that Xiao Yao San combined with anxiolytics was safe and effective for treating anxiety disorders. XYS alone also showed efficacy, though the authors called for larger-scale studies to better characterize adverse events.",
      "url": "",
      "periodical": "Wang Y, Chen X, Wei W, et al. Frontiers in Pharmacology. 2023; 14:1169292."
    },
    {
      "id": 33,
      "formula_id": 10,
      "title": "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis: XYS for Hypertension (2019)",
      "description": "A review of 17 randomized trials including 1,460 hypertensive patients found that adding Xiao Yao San to standard antihypertensive drugs improved blood pressure, anxiety and depression scores, and lipid profiles compared to antihypertensive drugs alone. The benefits appeared strongest for hypertension accompanied by emotional stress.",
      "url": "",
      "periodical": "Xiong X, Wang P, Duan L, et al. Phytomedicine. 2019; 61:152849."
    },
    {
      "id": 34,
      "formula_id": 10,
      "title": "Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis: XYS for Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (2023)",
      "description": "A review of RCTs assessing XYS for PCOS found that combining XYS with conventional medicines improved ovulation and pregnancy rates and decreased fasting insulin and insulin resistance in PCOS patients. The authors cautioned that significant heterogeneity and methodological shortcomings require careful interpretation.",
      "url": "",
      "periodical": "Zhou X, Ma Q, Yan Z, et al. Journal of Ethnopharmacology. 2023; 313:116517."
    },
    {
      "id": 35,
      "formula_id": 10,
      "title": "Narrative Review: Antidepressant Effects and Bioactive Ingredients of XYS (2023)",
      "description": "This comprehensive review summarized both preclinical and clinical evidence for XYS in depression. Key antidepressant mechanisms identified include regulation of monoamine neurotransmitters (serotonin, norepinephrine), modulation of the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis, improvement of synaptic plasticity, and anti-neuroinflammatory effects. Active compounds include saikosaponins from Chai Hu, paeoniflorin from Bai Shao, and glycyrrhizic acid from Gan Cao.",
      "url": "",
      "periodical": "Wang YT, Wang XL, Wang ZZ, Lei L, Hu D, Zhang Y. Phytomedicine. 2023; 109:154558."
    }
  ],
